/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-13T08:29:46Z","updated_at":"2025-01-13T08:31:12Z","body":"> The panel looks nice (tested on PC). What more is planned for this feature? Right now it's probably fine as a base.\r\n\r\nYes, base is ready. I just need to add few more action buttons and an option to lock the panel position.\r\n\r\n\r\n> Though I think the undo/redo buttons should get disabled when not available (similar to buttons in Scene menu).\r\n\r\nDisabling it for the `scene editor` is straightforward since it has a history_changed signal. However, it seems like there's no signal for the `script editor`. I’m looking for a way to detect if the script editor is currently open and whether undo/redo actions are available without using `has_undo` or `has_redo` for each change.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2586480536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590215858","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100339#issuecomment-2590215858","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100339","id":2590215858,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6aY46y","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoB